1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,003
Welcome to the student workflow in Circuit Studio Mastery.

2
00:00:04,253 --> 00:00:08,596
Enter your own name, student identifier, and course section when prompted.

3
00:00:08,846 --> 00:00:11,577
The name shown here is demonstration data.

4
00:00:11,827 --> 00:00:15,072
Your learning records are stored locally in this browser.

5
00:00:15,322 --> 00:00:18,895
They are not automatically sent to your instructor or to GitHub.

6
00:00:21,695 --> 00:00:26,793
Open Progress in the top toolbar, or use the floating activity and progress button.

7
00:00:27,043 --> 00:00:28,413
Choose your module.

8
00:00:28,663 --> 00:00:32,780
Completion reports which required activities have passed their checks.

9
00:00:33,030 --> 00:00:36,953
Concept mastery summarizes evidence across activities.

10
00:00:37,203 --> 00:00:42,813
In this version, Mastered requires unaided success on two different activities at least one

11
00:00:42,813 --> 00:00:43,614
day apart.

12
00:00:43,864 --> 00:00:47,853
Finishing one item is not the same as mastering every concept.

13
00:00:50,653 --> 00:00:53,872
Open an activity to see its completion checklist.

14
00:00:54,122 --> 00:00:56,855
For video learning, use the embedded player.

15
00:00:57,105 --> 00:01:01,309
Five questions appear after the required video playback is completed.

16
00:01:01,559 --> 00:01:03,365
Pass at least four out of five.

17
00:01:03,615 --> 00:01:06,315
Opening the lesson alone does not complete it.

18
00:01:06,565 --> 00:01:11,868
If playback is unavailable, contact your instructor rather than assuming that waiting will

19
00:01:11,868 --> 00:01:13,092
pass the activity.

20
00:01:15,892 --> 00:01:19,261
Practice activities can contain multiple examples.

21
00:01:19,511 --> 00:01:23,980
Check each answer and use the activity checklist to find what is still missing.

22
00:01:24,230 --> 00:01:28,763
Viewing an answer or leaving a tab open does not demonstrate completion.

23
00:01:29,013 --> 00:01:34,185
Active time is an estimate and pauses when the page is hidden, paused, or idle.

24
00:01:34,435 --> 00:01:37,634
Use the checks and your understanding to guide progress.

25
00:01:40,434 --> 00:01:45,584
For breadboard work, build the assigned circuit yourself, check placement, and verify

26
00:01:45,584 --> 00:01:46,013
wiring.

27
00:01:46,263 --> 00:01:49,346
Turn power on and connect valid measurement probes.

28
00:01:49,596 --> 00:01:51,432
Use Check and save measurement.

29
00:01:51,682 --> 00:01:57,367
In Principles, explain the reading using the relevant circuit principle, then submit this

30
00:01:57,367 --> 00:01:58,241
activity locally.

31
00:01:58,491 --> 00:02:00,766
Prediction writing has been removed.

32
00:02:01,016 --> 00:02:07,079
Build for me and automatic construction count as assistance, so restart for an independent

33
00:02:07,079 --> 00:02:07,512
attempt.

34
00:02:10,312 --> 00:02:13,609
Click the yellow Save progress button in the floating tool.

35
00:02:13,859 --> 00:02:16,593
You do not need to finish the current activity first.

36
00:02:16,843 --> 00:02:19,833
Save the JSON file in a folder you can find.

37
00:02:20,083 --> 00:02:23,762
It holds the learning record and saved work across modules.

38
00:02:24,012 --> 00:02:28,312
This is different from saving only the circuit drawing through the File menu.

39
00:02:28,562 --> 00:02:31,677
Save a fresh backup before ending each study session.

40
00:02:34,477 --> 00:02:37,772
The Progress dashboard shows the latest backup status.

41
00:02:38,022 --> 00:02:43,135
Browser autosave helps when you return using the same browser profile and website.

42
00:02:43,385 --> 00:02:46,670
A downloaded JSON file is your separate backup.

43
00:02:46,920 --> 00:02:53,043
Clearing browser data, changing devices, or using private browsing can interrupt local

44
00:02:53,043 --> 00:02:53,554
continuity.

45
00:02:53,804 --> 00:02:57,346
Keep the latest file and do not edit its contents manually.

46
00:03:00,146 --> 00:03:05,858
To restore a backup, open Progress, choose Activity details, then select Load saved

47
00:03:05,858 --> 00:03:06,298
progress.

48
00:03:06,548 --> 00:03:11,006
Choose your downloaded JSON file and read the replacement confirmation.

49
00:03:11,256 --> 00:03:16,470
Loading restores that saved record; it does not merge newer work with an older backup.

50
00:03:16,720 --> 00:03:19,975
Save your current progress first if you need to preserve it.

51
00:03:22,775 --> 00:03:27,286
After loading, open Progress and check the module and activity records.

52
00:03:27,536 --> 00:03:29,961
Resume the activity you want to continue.

53
00:03:30,211 --> 00:03:33,433
A restored unfinished activity remains unfinished.

54
00:03:33,683 --> 00:03:37,831
Saving or loading never replaces the required learning checks.

55
00:03:38,081 --> 00:03:43,560
On another computer, use your own student information so that records are not mixed between

56
00:03:43,560 --> 00:03:43,926
students.

57
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:52,559
When ready to submit, save a fresh progress JSON and download the full performance report

58
00:03:52,559 --> 00:03:53,337
from Progress.

59
00:03:53,587 --> 00:03:59,836
The report includes module completion, active time, concept mastery, and recorded evidence.

60
00:04:00,086 --> 00:04:01,922
Open the report to review it.

61
00:04:02,172 --> 00:04:06,609
Use Print or Save as PDF if your instructor requests a PDF.

62
00:04:06,859 --> 00:04:10,294
Written explanations still require instructor review.

63
00:04:13,094 --> 00:04:17,148
Finally, open the Canvas assignment specified by your instructor.

64
00:04:17,398 --> 00:04:23,405
Attach the latest JSON progress file and the report in the requested format, then complete

65
00:04:23,405 --> 00:04:26,208
the Canvas submission and check its confirmation.

66
00:04:26,458 --> 00:04:29,222
This video does not access your Canvas account.

67
00:04:29,472 --> 00:04:35,507
Clicking Submit this activity in Circuit Studio only saves the activity locally; it does not

68
00:04:35,507 --> 00:04:36,713
upload to Canvas.
